# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS for the ladder shapes home and land (v25 prep draft, 10-23).
# Syntax: header of build.py, plus the v25 keys shape:, kind:, rungs:, fork: (moments) and aim:, cost: (options),
# aims-shape.md section 4. Pours into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib (POUR-NOTES.md). Nothing built or run.
# Every moment: the five one-colour ways and one full cross cycle (s1 W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W, s2 W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U).
# home rungs: 0 a bond, 1 a household, 2 the household holds, 3 the centre of the line. Its "contest" is a test: a hard
#   winter for the household, a family crisis weathered together ({aim.contest} names it). Fields: love (a promise
#   for life, marrying well, a quick mind, loving with everything, protecting the ones I love), line (a family that
#   holds, the family name, children who question, a big loud family, the family's ways, many grandchildren, where
#   we come from), home (a home that runs well, our own roof, a home everyone is welcome in), and taking in a child.
#   A household's troubles are money, room, illness, distance and disagreement, never violence, neglect or abuse.
#   Only the low practice comes under 12, as a child's part in a household (no money, no romance, no nights out).
# land rungs: 0 tending, 1 keeping, 2 stewarding (the 30 ways of land.json and the land fields use rungs 0 to 2). Its
#   "contest" is a show or a harvest fair ({aim.contest} names it: a match, a race, a count for some ways). Fields: the
#   family land, wild living, farming, a street garden, the perfect garden, an animal sanctuary, champion horses, and
#   the 30 ways (allotments, bees, timber, wild swimming, fishing, the flood warden, a kiosk by the water and the rest).
#   Weather, water, soil, growth and animals act; the land never judges or approves; people read meaning into it.
#   Land moments are 12 and over.
# Ways in (practice, contest, chance, mentor): home rungs 0 to 3 and land rungs 0 to 2 each have four, one a practice.
# No integrate moments here (the Library writes those separately).

# ================================================================ HOME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, practice, rungs 0 1 (cycle s1)

== an ordinary week in the household
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: home, family
horizon: week
roles: parent, grandparent, sibling, friend
earth: an ordinary week at home: meals, chores, and the evening when everyone is in
tribal: an ordinary turn of the moon at the family's shelter: water fetched, the fire kept, everyone back by dark
magic: an ordinary week in a household of the realm: the hearth charm renewed, the meals, the lamp lit at dusk
scene: The week has its own shape at home: who cooks, who fixes, who calls whom at the end of the day. {N} has a part in it, and {aim.doing} is made of weeks like this far more than of big days.
scene tribal: The shelter runs on small jobs: water, wood, the fire, the evening meal. {N} has a share of them, and the family notices who does theirs.
scene magic: The household runs on small things: the hearth charm renewed each morning, the meals, the lamp lit at dusk. {N} has a share of it, and the old house seems to settle when it is done.
- W | keep the shared meal to its day and its hour, however tired everyone is | v: tradition, conformity | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U | ask everyone what the week needs, and fix the part that keeps going wrong | v: self-direction, benevolence | aim: work | foot: lesson asking first saves arguments | chance: 75
- B | take one job at home and make it plainly their own | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 85
- R | turn a dull evening into a game night, and ask {friend} round | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- G | help {grandparent} do things the way they always did | v: tradition, benevolence | aim: work | foot: lesson the old way has its reasons | chance: 85
- W>U | write the household's jobs on a list by the door, and keep to it | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 80
- U>B | learn the one repair that everyone else at home avoids | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B>R | strike a deal to swap the dull job for the fun one, this week only | v: power, stimulation | aim: ease | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 80
- R>G | bring everyone outside for the evening, whatever the weather | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 75
- G>W | let the week run itself for once, and just be part of it | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 85
works: The week holds its shape, and somebody says at dinner that it is good to be home.
works: Nobody notices anything special, which is the point: the house simply works, and {N} is part of why.
fails: The week comes apart by the middle, and everyone eats at different times again.
fails: {N} does their part, and nobody seems to see it; the house is busy with its own worries.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, practice, rungs 2 3 (cycle s2)

== the long table, years on
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: practice
rungs: 2 3
fork:
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: family, home
horizon: months
roles: child, partner, sibling, elder
earth: years in, the household others count on: birthdays remembered, the spare room ready, the call at the right time
tribal: years in, the fire the whole kin comes back to: the stores counted, the stories kept, the young ones fed
magic: years in, the hall the whole house comes back to: the wards renewed, the names remembered, the long table set
scene: Years in, {aim.doing} has become something others lean on: the house people come back to, the one who remembers the dates, the voice that calls at the right moment. It takes more keeping than it looks, and this year {N} feels the weight of it.
scene tribal: The kin come back to {Ns} fire from every camp now. Someone has to count the stores, keep the stories and feed whoever walks in, and it is mostly {N}.
scene magic: The house's long table seats three generations now, and the old wards on the door want renewing. {N} keeps all of it going, and is starting to wonder for how long.
- W | keep every birthday, call and gathering on its date, as always | v: tradition, conformity | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
- U | write down how the household runs, so it does not live only in one head | v: self-direction, security | aim: work | foot: lesson written ways outlast memory | chance: 75
- B | ask the grown ones to take a fixed share, and hold them to it | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 60
- R | throw a gathering for no reason at all, and fill the house | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: work | foot: means money-.04; person friend | chance: 75
- G | hand one of the family's ways to {child}, slowly, by doing it together | v: tradition, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- W>B | set the family's calendar for the year and give everyone their part | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: means freedom-.03 | chance: 65
- U>R | try a new way of meeting, a trip together instead of the same table | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: means money-.05 | chance: 60
- B>G | let the grown children host this year, and keep your hands off | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means time+.05 | chance: 65
- R>W | step back for a season and let the house be quieter | v: hedonism, security | aim: ease | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 85
- G>U | sit with the oldest ones and learn what they still remember | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 85
works: The house fills on the day, the way it does, and the youngest already know where everything goes.
works: Someone else picks up a thread {N} used to carry alone, without being asked.
fails: Fewer come this year, each with a good reason, and the table looks long.
fails: {N} keeps it all going and is worn thin by the end of it; the thanks come late.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, contest (a test), rungs 0 1 (cycle s1)

== when {aim.contest} comes to the household
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: contest
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: home, money, family
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, sibling, friend
earth: a hard winter for the household: hours cut at work, the heating failing, everyone home and short of room
tribal: a hard winter for the shelter: the herds thin, the stores low, everyone close round one fire
magic: a hard winter for the household: the hearth charm failing, the larder low, everyone in the one warm room
scene: It is {aim.contest}, the first real one: money runs short, work is uncertain, and everyone {N} shares a roof with is tired and short of room. How the household comes through it will be talked about for years, one way or another.
scene tribal: The herds are thin and the stores are low, and the whole shelter sits close round one fire. The elders say a family shows what it is in the lean months.
scene magic: The hearth charm is failing, the larder is low, and the whole household lives in the one warm room. The neighbours are watching to see which houses hold.
- W | draw up a strict budget together, and everyone keeps to it | v: security, conformity | aim: try | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 65
- U | look into every grant, swap and saving there is, and use them | v: self-direction, security | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | take on extra work and carry the household through yourself | v: achievement, power | aim: try | foot: means money+.05; means health-.04 | chance: 55
- R | keep spirits up with music, games and a feast made of almost nothing | v: hedonism, stimulation | aim: try | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 60
- G | ask the neighbours and the wider family to pool what they have | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: try | foot: person neighbour | chance: 65
- W>U | sit everyone down and plan the months ahead, week by week | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: try | foot: lesson a plan calms a house | chance: 70
- U>B | sell what the household can spare, and drive a hard bargain | v: achievement, power | aim: try | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 65
- B>R | keep the trouble to yourself and act as if all is well | v: power, hedonism | aim: skip | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 50
- R>G | take everyone to stay with the wider family for the worst weeks | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: skip | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 70
- G>W | keep your head down, keep things as they are, and let it pass | v: security, tradition | aim: skip | foot: lesson hard seasons do pass | chance: 80
works: The household comes out of the lean months thinner, closer, and a little proud of itself.
works: It is hard all the way through, but nobody is left to carry it alone, and that is remembered.
fails: The months grind on, tempers fray, and the household comes through it, but only just.
fails: The money runs out before the trouble does, and the spring starts with debts to pay.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, contest (a test), rungs 2 3 (cycle s2)

== the season the whole family is tested
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: contest
rungs: 2 3
fork:
stages: adult mature elder
age: 35-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: family, home, health
horizon: months
roles: parent, child, sibling, partner
earth: a family crisis weathered together: an illness in the older generation and a job lost in the younger, in one season
tribal: a hard season for the whole kin: an elder failing and a young hunter's luck gone, both at once
magic: a hard season for the whole house: an elder's sight failing and a young one's apprenticeship ended, both at once
scene: This is {aim.contest}, and it comes when nobody planned it: the oldest of the family needs looking after, one of the younger ones has lost their work and needs a room, and the bills do not wait. The whole family is watching how {Ns} household holds, and so is {N}.
scene tribal: The oldest of the kin can no longer walk to the river, and a young hunter has come back with nothing three moons running. Everyone looks to {Ns} fire.
scene magic: The house's eldest is losing their sight, and a young one's apprenticeship has ended without a place. The family gathers in {Ns} hall to see what will be done.
- W | call the family together and share out the care fairly, on a rota | v: conformity, universalism | aim: try | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- U | find out every kind of help there is, and get the right one in | v: self-direction, security | aim: try | foot: place care.houses | chance: 65
- B | take the decisions yourself, quickly, and answer for them | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 55
- R | move everyone in together for the season and make it loud and warm | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: means ties+.06; means freedom-.04 | chance: 55
- G | take the oldest one in, and do the caring as it was once done for them | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: try | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 60
- W>B | set the rules for the shared house, and see that they are kept | v: conformity, power | aim: try | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 60
- U>R | let the crisis run its course, and step in only where you are needed | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: skip | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 70
- B>G | pay for help from outside so the family can stay a family | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: try | foot: means money-.08 | chance: 70
- R>W | say plainly you cannot carry it this time, and ask someone else to lead | v: self-direction, security | aim: skip | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 75
- G>U | let each branch of the family handle its own part, and trust them | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: skip | foot: lesson trust lets others step up | chance: 70
works: The season is long, but the family comes through it on speaking terms, and some of it closer than before.
works: People who had drifted come back to help, and the house is fuller than it has been in years.
fails: The care falls unevenly, and an old grudge between two branches of the family wakes up again.
fails: The household holds, but {N} comes out of the season tired in a way that takes a year to lift.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, mentor, rungs 0 1 2 3 (cycle s1)

== the one who has kept a household before
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: mentor
rungs: 0 1 2 3
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: family, home, friends
horizon: months
roles: mentor, elder, grandparent
earth: an older person who has kept a household together through more than {N} has seen yet
tribal: an old one of the clan who has kept a fire going through more winters than anyone can count
magic: an old steward of the realm who has kept a great house standing through three reigns
scene: Down the road there is {aim.person}, who has kept a household going through more than {N} has seen yet, and who offers, half joking, to tell {N} where it usually goes wrong. The offer comes at the right moment: {N} has been {aim.doing} on instinct, and the instinct is running out.
scene tribal: The old woman of the next shelter has kept a fire going through more winters than anyone can count, and she has been watching how {N} does it.
scene magic: The old steward of the great house has kept it standing through three reigns, and sends word that {N} may come and ask questions.
- W | ask how they did it, and follow the advice to the letter for a year | v: tradition, conformity | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 80
- U | listen to everything, then keep only what fits your own house | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson take advice, keep judgement | chance: 75
- B | ask them to put in a word where it will open doors for the family | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: person patron | chance: 50
- R | invite them round and let the house speak for itself | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- G | visit them every week, and help with whatever they are doing | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
- W>U | ask them to sit down over the family's plans and accounts together | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- U>B | trade what you are good at for what they know | v: self-direction, power | aim: try | foot: person mentor | chance: 65
- B>R | thank them, and keep their number for a harder day | v: power, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
- R>G | bring the whole house along, and make an afternoon of it | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- G>W | take things slower, the way they wish they had at your age | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 85
works: The advice turns out to be right about almost everything, and kind about the rest.
works: One remark over a cup of tea saves {Ns} household a year of trouble.
fails: The advice belongs to another time, and half of it does not fit {Ns} house at all.
fails: The older one means well but talks over {N}, and the visits thin out.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, rival, rungs 1 2 3 (cycle s2)

== the other branch of the family
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: rival
rungs: 1 2 3
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: family, home, conflict
horizon: years
roles: rival, sibling, parent, elder
earth: a sibling or an in-law with their own idea of where the family gathers and whose ways it keeps
tribal: another hearth of the same kin, pulling the young ones and the feasts toward its own fire
magic: a cousin's house of the same blood, with a finer hall and its own claim on the family's feasts
scene: {rival} has their own idea of how the family should be: where it gathers, whose ways it keeps, whose word counts. This year both households want the big gathering, and the rest of the family is quietly picking sides.
scene tribal: Another hearth of the same kin keeps calling the young ones and the feasts to its own fire. {rival} tends it, and does not hide that it is meant as a challenge.
scene magic: {rival}'s house is of the same blood and has the finer hall, and this year it has sent out word of the midwinter feast before {N} could.
- W | propose taking turns, year by year, and write it down | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U | find out through someone they trust what {rival} really wants from it | v: self-direction, benevolence | aim: try | foot: person go-between | chance: 60
- B | make your gathering the one nobody will want to miss | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: means money-.05 | chance: 55
- R | have it out with {rival} face to face, and clear the air | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: try | foot: lesson saying it aloud clears the air | chance: 50
- G | let them have it this year, and keep the peace | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 85
- W>B | invite {rival} to run it together, and share the credit | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 60
- U>R | start a new day of your own that does not compete with theirs | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 70
- B>G | win over the oldest of the family first, and the rest will follow | v: power, tradition | aim: try | foot: person elder | chance: 55
- R>W | go to theirs with good grace, and bring the best dish | v: hedonism, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 80
- G>U | hold a smaller gathering of your own, the way you like it | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: place gather.house | chance: 80
works: The two households find a way to share the family, and the young ones get two tables instead of one.
works: {rival} gives a little ground, and {N} finds that giving some back costs less than expected.
fails: The family splits its year between two houses, and some cousins stop coming to either.
fails: The quarrel goes quiet but not away, and it surfaces again at the next big day.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, setback, rungs any (cycle s1)

== the hope that does not come this year
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: home, family, loss
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, friend, sibling
earth: something the household had built a year around falls through: a home lost at the last moment, a match that ends, a long hope that does not come
tribal: a hope the family had held all year does not come, and the elders say only that seasons turn
magic: a house promised to the family goes to another by the steward's word, and the plans made around it are unmade
scene: The thing {N} had built the year around falls through at the last moment, and nobody is to blame. The plan for {aim.thing} has a hole in it now, and the people at home are waiting, gently, to see what {N} does next.
scene tribal: The hope the family had held all year does not come, and the shelter is quiet about it. The elders say only that seasons turn.
scene magic: The house promised to the family has gone to another by the steward's word, and the plans made around it have to be unmade.
- W | pick the plan up where it broke, and start again on the same lines | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U | work out what went wrong, and what can be different next time | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | push harder, find another way in, and do not wait | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 55
- R | get away for a few days, then come back to it with fresh eyes | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 75
- G | lean on the people closest, and let them carry some of it | v: benevolence, security | aim: work | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 80
- W>U | ask someone who has been through the same how they went on | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 75
- U>B | set a new, smaller goal for this year that can really be reached | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson a smaller step still counts | chance: 75
- B>R | let this one go, and put the energy into your work for a while | v: power, stimulation | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 85
- R>G | stop chasing it, and give the time to the people already at home | v: hedonism, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson the people here still count | chance: 85
- G>W | let the hope rest, and stay close to the friend who stood by you | v: security, tradition | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
works: The household closes round the loss, and the next step, whatever it turns out to be, is easier to see.
works: In a few months the hole in the plan has become a shape {N} can work with.
fails: The loss sits heavy in the house for longer than anyone expected.
fails: {N} carries more of it alone than anyone knows, and the year is a hard one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, plateau, rungs 1 2 3, fork go_on (cycle s2)

== the household that runs on habit
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: plateau
rungs: 1 2 3
fork: go_on
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: home, family, partner
horizon: years
roles: partner, child, sibling, friend
earth: years of the same routine at home, and the feeling that {aim.thing} has stopped growing
tribal: seasons of the same round at the fire, and the sense that the kin is no longer growing closer
magic: years of the same rites in the house, and the sense that the household has stopped deepening
scene: Nothing is wrong at home, exactly. The days run the same way, the savings sit where they sat, the calls come on their dates and say the same things. A round birthday this year has {N} asking whether {aim.doing} should be pushed on, changed, eased off, or left as what it already is.
scene tribal: The kin meet at the same fire on the same nights and say the same things. As the moon turns, {N} wonders whether this is all it will be.
scene magic: The wards are renewed, the table set, the names said, year on year. The turning of the year asks every household for its vows again, and {N} has to decide what to say.
- W | keep every habit exactly as it is, since steadiness is the point | v: tradition, security | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U | change one thing that has gone stale, and see what follows | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson one change can wake a house | chance: 70
- B | set the household a goal for the year, and see that it is met | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 60
- R | shake it up with a move, a trip or a room made new | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | stop measuring for a while, and be glad of what holds | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 85
- W>B | take on a bigger family duty, such as an elder's care | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 55
- U>R | ask the others at home what they want next, and follow their lead | v: self-direction, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
- B>G | ease back for a year, and spend some of the time on yourself | v: achievement, security | aim: ease | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 85
- R>W | let it go, and put the hours into friends outside the house | v: self-direction, tradition | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G>U | let it go as a goal, and simply live in the home it has become | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: lesson it was already a home | chance: 90
works: Something shifts, small at first, and the house feels as if it is going somewhere again.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the year has a direction, and the others at home can feel it.
fails: The change does not take, and the old routine settles back like dust.
fails: The year slides by much like the last one, and the question waits for next year.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- home, cost, rungs 0 1 2, fork pay (cycle s1)

== what the household can afford
tier: life event
shape: home
kind: cost
rungs: 0 1 2
fork: pay
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-75
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: home, money, family
horizon: years
roles: partner, parent, child, sibling
earth: the price of {aim.doing}: a bigger place, time away from work, or the family's patience
tribal: the price of a bigger shelter: hides, labour, and the patience of the whole hearth
magic: the price of a bigger house: the steward's fee, a season's labour, and the household's patience
scene: This year {aim.doing} has a price, and it has come due all at once: the place is too small, and the deposit, the extra room or the time off work will cost more than the household has put by. Someone at home has started asking how long this goes on, and the answer is needed before the lease runs out in spring.
scene tribal: A bigger shelter would hold everyone, but it would take every hide the family has and a season of labour before the herds move. The hearth is tired of waiting.
scene magic: A larger house is offered for the steward's fee, payable by midsummer. It would take the household's savings and a season of everyone's labour, and patience is already thin.
